import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.PeriodTorusLineBundleClassificationUniquenessImaginary

/-!
# Uniqueness in the Appell--Humbert construction

The full unitary input data are determined by an actual analytic,
fibre-linear isomorphism of the constructed native line bundles.  The
scalar gauge is extracted from the original map and proved entire and
nonvanishing.  The semicharacter law also forces the imaginary form to be
integral on the genuine period lattice.

This family proves injectivity, not surjectivity for arbitrary native
holomorphic line bundles.  It does not assume a global holomorphic frame
on their universal-cover pullbacks, a factor normal-form theorem, or an
Appell--Humbert classification theorem.
-/
